# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — the `meta for` arm, and the
# HARDEST cell of the class: this one was a COMPILER ICE, not a runtime abort.
#
# `Stmt::MetaFor | Stmt::MetaWhile` is the fourth loop-shaped statement arm.
# Its pass 2 walked the live set IN PLACE while its three siblings cloned and
# unioned — the overwrite bug, surviving in the one arm an earlier sweep
# missed. With a ZERO-TRIP `meta for`, the assignment in the body is a KILL the
# expansion never emits: walked in place, it deleted `s` from the live set, the
# `v.push(s)` above it then read `s` as dead and emitted a move, and the
# `print(s)` below read the moved-out slot.
#
# Liveness runs on the UNEXPANDED AST — `compute_function_liveness` is called
# from the prescan in `src/ir/lowering/functions.rs` ~50 lines BEFORE meta
# expansion — so a `liveness.rs` comment claiming the meta forms "cannot
# themselves consume a runtime local" was false; it is corrected in the same
# commit (Core #14).
#
# AXIS CELL: loop kind = `meta for` · trip count = ZERO · body = an
# ASSIGN-KILL of a name consumed above and read below · name type = String
# (heap-forced).
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD, both lanes: `gg build` rc 101,
# `GIR validation errors: ... local _1 read after MoveZero`, panicking at
# `src/ir/lowering/mod.rs` (C and `--backend=llvm`). The byte-identical runtime
# twin `cow_for_zero_trip_body_kill_control.gg` is rc 0 and correct at pre-fix
# HEAD — that pair is what localises the defect to this one arm.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(s)
    meta for i in 0..0:
        s = mk("c", "d")
    print(s)
    print(v[0])
